@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] kvm-probe-no-elevation-or-output
The probe MUST run without setuid bits or file capabilities, MUST accept and
print nothing (arguments and environment cannot influence the verdict), and
MUST retain no state. Operational events belong to the caller's Lilly.Events
catalog, never to a helper-side diagnostic stream.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:assurance] kvm-probe-requires-real-vm-creation
The probe MUST report success only after opening /dev/kvm, observing API
version 12 and creating an empty VM; device-file existence or open permission
alone must not establish execution capability. The probe must run no guest
code. Real-device equivalence with the C predecessor is verified during
conversion; NixOS fixtures that boot the Lilly service on nested KVM exercise
the shipped probe through the ownership startup boundary.
